% A head variable that no positive body literal binds is an error.  Y is
% reported as a singleton as well, because it is a separate mistake rather
% than a consequence of the first.  A predicate name longer than 43 bytes is
% cut to 40 in a message and marked with "...": the first of the two long
% names below fits, and the second, a byte longer, is cut.
bar(a).
foo(X) :-
    bar(Y).
abcdefghijabcdefghijabcdefghijabcdefghijabc(X) :- bar(a).
abcdefghijabcdefghijabcdefghijabcdefghijabcd(X) :- bar(a).
